    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract, `AuditLogCapture` is a helper), and both tests pass along with a clean build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field: **SILVER** when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise **BRONZE**.\n\nSince `OwnerDto` is generated from the OpenAPI spec and derived owner fields (like `displayName`, `initials`) are computed in the MapStruct mapper, I followed that existing pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema (next to `membershipNumber`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a computed `@Mapping` for `membershipTier`:\n   ```java\n   owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount().intValue() == 0\n       && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isEmpty() ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\"\n   ```\n\nThe field is derived at serialization time from the already-persisted `namesakeCount` and `email`, so it's returned consistently on later reads without needing a new pipeline step or DB column.",
